        "original_id": "3dbf37ef-7f5e-5b43-a643-b3230f102d13",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Konstantin Somov, Andrey Ivanovich Somov, Alexandre Benois, Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov, Lyde Browne\n- Organizations: Hermitage Museum, Nevsky Pickwickians\n- Places: Saint Petersburg, Pavlovsk Palace\n- Concepts: 18th-century art, music, classical sculpture collections\n\nFacts:\n- The Hermitage Museum has been open to the public since 1852.\n- Konstantin Somov was born into the family of Andrey Ivanovich Somov, a major art historian and Hermitage Museum curator.\n- Konstantin Somov became interested in 18th-century art and music at an early age.\n- The Nevsky Pickwickians originally included Alexandre Benois, Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov, and Konstantin Somov, with Alexandre Benois effectively serving as the group's leader.\n- The former collection of Lyde Browne now forms the majority of the classical sculpture collections of the Hermitage Museum in Saint Petersburg and Pavlovsk Palace in the city's suburbs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
