        "text": "Page: Konstantin Somov. Sentence: Born into a family of a major art historian and Hermitage Museum curator Andrey Ivanovich Somov, he became interested in 18th-century art and music at an early age.\nPage: Hermitage Museum. Sentence: It has been open to the public since 1852.\nPage: Nevsky Pickwickians. Sentence: The group originally included Alexandre Benois (effectively its leader), Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov and Konstantin Somov.\nPage: Lyde Browne (antiquary). Sentence: This now forms the majority of the classical sculpture collections of the Hermitage Museum in Saint Petersburg and the Pavlovsk Palace in the city's suburbs.",
